@* Decision 0011 (run W4, unit R9): the mockups' "Open folder" button of Settings › Data & storage. It names a target (and for a workspace its
   run and slot), never a path; data.js POSTs it to /api/data/open, which resolves the folder on the server and starts the file manager of
   this machine. Disabled, with why, when the folder doesn't exist yet or opening folders is turned off. Model: DataOpenButton. *@
@using PiSharp.WebAgent.DataStorage
@model DataOpenButton
<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary flex-shrink-0" type="button" data-open-folder="@Model.Target" data-run="@Model.Run" data-slot="@Model.Slot"
        aria-label="@Model.Label" title="@(Model.Disabled ?? Model.Label)" disabled="@(Model.Disabled is not null)"><i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="d-none d-sm-inline ms-1">Open folder</span></button>
